"},"$:/plugins/richlink/macro":{"title":"$:/plugins/richlink/macro","tags":"$:/tags/Macro","text":"\define abevregexp() ^(?:(?:[a-z]{2,3}|m)\.)?([a-zA-Z0-9_]{5}).*

\define domainLinks()
<$list filter="""[<link>split[://]last[]search-replace::regexp[www.],[]search-replace::regexp<abevregexp>,[@$1]] +[limit[1]]""" >
    <$list filter="[all[shadows+tiddlers]prefix[$:/plugins/richlink/d]search:title:{!!title}]">
        <$tiddler tiddler={{!!title}}>
            <$transclude/>
        </$tiddler>
        <$list-empty>
            <$tiddler tiddler="$:/plugins/richlink/iframe">
                <$transclude/>
            </$tiddler>
        </$list-empty>
    </$list>
</$list>
\end

\define applytemplate(signum)
<$list filter="[all[shadows+tiddlers]prefix[$:/plugins/richlink/f]search:title:[$signum$]]" emptyMessage=<<domainLinks>>>
    <$tiddler tiddler={{!!title}}>
        <$transclude/>
    </$tiddler>
</$list>
\end

\define richlink(link, 1, 2, 3, 4)

<$vars command="$link$">

<!-- FORCED IFRAME MODE -->
<$list filter="[<command>match[iframe]]">
    <$vars
        iframe-url="$1$"
        iframe-description="$2$"
        iframe-site="$3$"
        iframe-height="$4$">
        <$tiddler tiddler="$:/plugins/richlink/iframe">
            <$transclude/>
        </$tiddler>
    </$vars>
</$list>

<!-- NORMAL MODE -->
<$list filter="[<command>!match[iframe]]">
    <$vars link="$link$" 1="$1$" 2="$2$" 3="$3$" 4="$4$">
        <$list filter="""[<link>split[.]last[]addprefix[@]] [<link>split[://]last[]search-replace::regexp[www.],[]search-replace::regexp<abevregexp>,[@$1]] +[limit[1]]""" >
            <$macrocall $name=applytemplate signum={{!!title}} />
        </$list>
    </$vars>
</$list>

</$vars>
\end

<$list filter="[all[current]has[richlink]get[richlink]]" variable="link">
{{$:/core/images/import-button}}<$macrocall $name=richlink link=<<link>>/>
</$list>"},"$:/plugins/richlink/richlink-styles":{"title":"$:/plugins/richlink/richlink-styles","tags":"$:/tags/Stylesheet","type":"text/vnd.tiddlywiki","text":"/* Palette-reactive styling for the richlink plugin.
   All colours come from the active TiddlyWiki palette via <<colour ...>>. */

/* ---- Generic richlink card shell ---- */

.rl-iframe-card,
.rl-txt {
    display: block;
    max-width: 48em;
    margin: 0.35em 0;
    padding: 0.45em 0.55em;
    border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-border>>;
    border-radius: 0.45em;
    background: <<colour background>>;
    color: <<colour foreground>>;
}

.rl-iframe-credit {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.35em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 0.45em;
}

.rl-txt-fallback a {
    color: <<colour primary>>;
    text-decoration: none;
    word-break: break-word;
}

.rl-txt-fallback a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
}

/* ---- GitHub issue button ---- */

.gh-issue {
    display: inline;
    border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-border>>;
    padding: 0px 0px 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-right: 5px;
    background: <<colour background>>;
}

.gh-issue a.tc-tiddlylink-external {
    color: <<colour foreground>>;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 80%;
}

.gh-issue:hover a.tc-tiddlylink-external {
    color: <<colour primary>>;
    text-decoration: underline;
}

.gh-issue svg {
    width: .9em;
    vertical-align: -.65em;
    fill: currentColor;
}

/* ---- Wikipedia link ---- */

.rl-wikipedia {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.28em;
    color: <<colour primary>>;
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
    line-height: 1.2;
}

.rl-wikipedia:hover .rl-wikipedia-title {
    text-decoration: underline;
}

.rl-wikipedia-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 1em;
    height: 1em;
    color: <<colour muted-foreground>>;
    transform: translateY(0.12em);
    flex: 0 0 auto;
}

.rl-wikipedia-icon svg {
    width: 1em;
    height: 1em;
    fill: currentColor;
    vertical-align: middle;
}

.rl-wikipedia-title {
    color: <<colour primary>>;
}

/* ---- TiddlyWiki docs button ---- */

.twd {
    display: inline;
    margin-right: 5px;
    border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-border>>;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 1px 0px 1px 5px;
    background: <<colour background>>;
    font-size: 80%;
}

.twd a.tc-tiddlylink-external {
    color: <<colour foreground>>;
    text-decoration: none;
}

.twd a.tc-tiddlylink-external:hover {
    color: <<colour primary>>;
    text-decoration: underline;
}

.twd svg {
    width: 1em;
    vertical-align: bottom;
    fill: currentColor;
}

/* ---- Embedded media (YouTube / audio / video) ---- */

.rich-iframe {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    height: auto;
    border: 0;
}

.richlink-audio,
.richlink-video {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
}

/* ---- Text card ---- */

.rl-txt-frame-wrap {
    border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-border>>;
    border-radius: 0.4em;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: <<colour page-background>>;
    color: <<colour foreground>> !important;
}

.rl-txt-body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.6em 0.8em;
    max-height: 100%;
    overflow: auto;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: <<colour foreground>> !important;
    background: <<colour background>> !important;
}

.rl-txt-fallback {
    margin-top: 0.35em;
    font-size: 0.8em;
    color: <<colour muted-foreground>>;
    word-break: break-all;
}

/* ---- Image card ---- */

.richlink-img {
    display: inline-block;
    background: <<colour background>>;
    margin: 0 0 27px 30px;
    padding: 10px 10px 15px;
    text-align: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: <<colour foreground>>;
    font-size: 18px;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.55);
}

.richlink-img a {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: none;
}

.richlink-img img {
    display: block;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
}

.richlink-img-caption {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    color: <<colour muted-foreground>>;
    font-size: 0.8em;
}

/* ---- Generic iframe card ---- */

.rl-iframe-credit,
.rl-iframe-title,
.rl-iframe-site,
.rl-iframe-by {
    color: <<colour muted-foreground>>;
    font-size: 13px;
}

.rl-iframe-title,
.rl-iframe-site {
    text-decoration: none;
}

.rl-iframe-title:hover,
.rl-iframe-site:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
}

.rl-iframe-wrap {
    border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-border>>;
    border-radius: 0.4em;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: <<colour page-background>>;
}

.rl-iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
}

.rl-iframe-empty {
    color: <<colour muted-foreground>>;
    font-size: 0.9em;
}
"},"$:/plugins/richlink/txtviewer-widget.js":{"title":"$:/plugins/richlink/txtviewer-widget.js","type":"application/javascript","module-type":"widget","text":"/*\
title: $:/plugins/richlink/txtviewer-widget.js
type: application/javascript
module-type: widget
\*/

(function(){

"use strict";

var Widget = require("$:/core/modules/widgets/widget.js").widget;

/*
Resolve a palette colour the same way <<colour>> does:
$:/palette (dictionary tiddler) -> $:/palettes/Vanilla -> $:/config/DefaultColourMappings/<name>.
Values that reference other colours (<<colour x>>) are resolved recursively.
Never throws: returns "" on any failure so callers simply skip the inline style.
*/
function paletteColour(name) {
    try {
        var wiki = $tw.wiki,
            visited = {},
            resolve = function(value) {
                if(typeof value !== "string") {
                    return "";
                }
                var m = value.match(/^<<colour\s+([^>]+)>>\s*$/);
                if(m && !visited[m[1]]) {
                    visited[m[1]] = true;
                    return paletteColour(m[1]);
                }
                return value;
            },
            lookup = function(title) {
                var t = wiki.getTiddler(title);
                if(!t || typeof t.fields.text !== "string") {
                    return undefined;
                }
                var re = new RegExp("^" + name.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&") + "\\s*:\\s*(.*)$", "m");
                var m = t.fields.text.match(re);
                return m ? m[1].trim() : undefined;
            };
        var val = lookup(wiki.getTiddlerText("$:/palette"));
        if(val === undefined) {
            val = lookup("$:/palettes/Vanilla");
        }
        if(val === undefined) {
            val = wiki.getTiddlerText("$:/config/DefaultColourMappings/" + name);
        }
        return resolve(val || "");
    } catch(e) {
        return "";
    }
}

var TxtViewerWidget = function(parseTreeNode,options) {
    this.initialise(parseTreeNode,options);
};

TxtViewerWidget.prototype = new Widget();

TxtViewerWidget.prototype.render = function(parent,nextSibling) {
    this.parentDomNode = parent;
    this.computeAttributes();
    this.execute();

    var foreground = paletteColour("foreground"),
        background = paletteColour("background"),
        pageBackground = paletteColour("page-background"),
        border = paletteColour("tiddler-border");

    var container = this.document.createElement("div");
    container.className = "rl-txt-frame-wrap";
    container.style.height = this.height || "300px";
    container.style.overflow = "hidden";
    container.style.border = "1px solid " + border;
    container.style.borderRadius = "0.4em";
    container.style.background = pageBackground;
    parent.insertBefore(container,nextSibling);
    this.domNodes.push(container);

    var self = this;

    // Iframes are not subject to CORS, so this always displays the document —
    // used when the cross-origin fetch is blocked by the host.
    function renderIframeFallback() {
        container.innerHTML = "";
        var frame = self.document.createElement("iframe");
        frame.src = self.src;
        frame.style.display = "block";
        frame.style.width = "100%";
        frame.style.height = "100%";
        frame.style.border = "0";
        // The embedded document is cross-origin, so we can't style its contents —
        // it renders with browser defaults. Force a solid light background and
        // light color-scheme so the default black text stays readable over the
        // dark card.
        frame.style.background = "#ffffff";
        frame.style.colorScheme = "light";
        frame.setAttribute("loading","lazy");
        container.appendChild(frame);
    }

    if(!self.src) {
        container.textContent = "No text source supplied";
        return;
    }

    container.textContent = "Loading text…";

    fetch(self.src,{mode:"cors",credentials:"omit"}).then(function(response) {
        if(!response.ok) {
            throw new Error("HTTP " + response.status);
        }
        return response.text();
    }).then(function(text) {
        // Success — render the text inline, styled by the active palette.
        // Colours are applied inline so nothing in the host app can override them.
        container.innerHTML = "";
        var pre = self.document.createElement("pre");
        pre.className = "rl-txt-body";
        pre.style.margin = "0";
        pre.style.padding = "0.6em 0.8em";
        pre.style.maxHeight = "100%";
        pre.style.overflow = "auto";
        pre.style.whiteSpace = "pre-wrap";
        pre.style.wordBreak = "break-word";
        pre.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
        pre.style.fontSize = "0.9em";
        pre.style.lineHeight = "1.45";
        if(foreground) {
            pre.style.color = foreground;
        }
        if(background) {
            pre.style.background = background;
        }
        pre.textContent = text;
        container.appendChild(pre);
    }).catch(function() {
        renderIframeFallback();
    });
};

TxtViewerWidget.prototype.execute = function() {
    this.src = this.getAttribute("src","");
    this.height = this.getAttribute("height","300px");
    this.makeChildWidgets();
};

TxtViewerWidget.prototype.refresh = function(changedTiddlers) {
    var changedAttributes = this.computeAttributes();
    if(changedAttributes.src || changedAttributes.height) {
        this.refreshSelf();
        return true;
    }
    return this.refreshChildren(changedTiddlers);
};

exports.txtviewer = TxtViewerWidget;

})();
"},"$:/plugins/xyvir/lithic-richlinks/readme":{"title":"$:/plugins/xyvir/lithic-richlinks/readme","tags":"","text":"!Lithic Richlinks

Displays external links as rich objects. Type:

```
<<richlink "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID">>
```

and the link is replaced by an embedded player, viewer or styled link depending on what it points to. One command, many shapes — the URL itself picks the template:

* Domain templates (e.g. `d@youtube`, `d@github`, `d@wikipedia`, `d@soundcloud`, `d@jsfiddle`, `d@disq.us`, `d@twitter`, `docs@tiddlywiki`)
* File templates (e.g. `f@txt`, `fimg@jpg@jpeg@png@gif@webp@svg`, `faudio@mp3@ogg@wav@flac`, `fvideo@mp4@avi@webm@ogv`)
* Generic [[$:/plugins/richlink/iframe]] template as a fallback

!Extra parameters

Some templates accept extra parameters after the URL, e.g. an image caption or an iframe height:

```
<<richlink "https://example.com/photo.jpg" "my caption">>
<<richlink iframe "https://example.com/page" "description" "site" "600px">>
```

Within a template the URL is available as `<<link>>` and the extra parameters as `<<1>>`, `<<2>>`, `<<3>>` and `<<4>>`.

!In the editor

Type `/richlinks` in the editor to insert `<<richlink "">>` with the caret placed inside the quotes — just paste a URL.

!Test links

Verified embed-friendly URLs for each template:

```
<<richlink "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ">>                          <!-- d@youtube     -->
<<richlink "https://github.com/Jermolene/TiddlyWiki5">>                            <!-- d@github      -->
<<richlink "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TiddlyWiki">>                            <!-- d@wikipedia   -->
<<richlink "https://example.com/">>                                               <!-- iframe fallback -->
<<richlink iframe "https://www.openstreetmap.org/export/embed.html?bbox=-0.004,51.476,0.006,51.482&amp;layer=mapnik" "OpenStreetMap" "openstreetmap.org" "450px">>  <!-- forced iframe -->
```

Iframe-embeddable targets (no `X-Frame-Options` / CSP `frame-ancestors` block): `example.com`, the OpenStreetMap / YouTube / Vimeo / Bing Maps embed endpoints, and Wikipedia pages.

!Notes

* The tweet template renders tweets via the official Twitter plugin when installed, and falls back to a plain link otherwise.
* Text files are fetched and rendered inline with palette colours when the host allows CORS (e.g. `raw.githubusercontent.com`); otherwise they fall back to an unstyled iframe.
* SoundCloud only embeds track/set URLs (e.g. `https://soundcloud.com/zedd/clarity-1`), not the homepage.
* Based on the [[RichLinks revisited demosite|https://richlinkrevistedii.tiddlyhost.com/]] by Mat von TWaddle and JanJo.
"}}}
